                "entry_id": "1ccd0877-1ac2-368c-9e54-4f395006a863",
                "word": "dunderhead",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b2dbae6e-eae9-4a72-961e-8e0cffccfe4a",
                        "entry_id": "1ccd0877-1ac2-368c-9e54-4f395006a863",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dunderheads"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e46ccff9-7cd5-3251-a959-2811f4bbcf2c",
                        "entry_id": "1ccd0877-1ac2-368c-9e54-4f395006a863",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A stupid person; a dunce."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c1a61fe-4e3b-4d4f-8a52-3d4aea0d5113",
                                "sense_id": "e46ccff9-7cd5-3251-a959-2811f4bbcf2c",
                                "text": "You're the stupidest dunderhead I ever saw or ever heard of, so help me Moses!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0f4122f-96db-4834-ae27-457287b99b3e",
                                "sense_id": "e46ccff9-7cd5-3251-a959-2811f4bbcf2c",
                                "text": "Poor old fellow's a dunderhead. That's where it is in a nutshell. Never could make a living. […] Nice old chap as ever lived. Only impractical, dreamy. Gentle as a sheep—and no more capable of running that big, expensive plant than a motherly old ewe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7070bccf-c418-4d68-90f4-7d37d2b855a9",
                                "sense_id": "e46ccff9-7cd5-3251-a959-2811f4bbcf2c",
                                "text": "Cheney & Company swooned over Mr. Chalabi because he was telling them what they wanted to hear. . . . A half-dozen dunderheads who thought they knew everything assumed they could control Mr. Chalabi and use him as the instrument of their utopian fantasies."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
